Objective Comment:
In addition to mid-year comments;
-additional support to Project Cortina during Q4 as deal potentially back on.  Additional input provided during November.
- supported Fran and Raj in structured interviews with GSA female group and support to then establish 'Go Connect' - an initiative to improve dialogue and networking for women in the team to improve engagement and sponsorship of issues raised. Regular calls take place, combination of facilitated discussion on guest speaker.   For example, the most recent call focused on leadsership team feedback on unconscious bias.  Mentoring is now likely to be a follow up to this intitiative and has not yet been formally implemented.

In additio to mid-year review;
- 2019 EES score declined by 3 on 'like for like' basis, likely impacted by the decision not to hold a full team F2F meeting in Q3 (this was highly valued last year).
- Team remain highly commited to buidling employee engagement which remains a regular agenda item.

In additiona to mid year comments;
- Successful implementation of 'part 1' Legal Entity Integration project for the UK on 1 November.  Consultation completed without issues, ensrued full coordination between HR, MBS, Finance and IT to minimise risks and a ensure successful outcome.  Process will provide a model for 'part 2' of the project in mid 2020.
- In preparation for new HR model, F2F meeting of UK HR team held in November including a facilitated Insights session focusing on the needs of the team during the transition and discussion around how to support each other.  The team also began to work on ideas to ensure the new model works effectively in the short term and opportunitiies to work in a lesss siloed approach to address 'local' key issues.

